The City reported, among others, the following significant accomplishments in CY 2024:
a. The City was awarded Seal of Local Good Governance from the Department of Interior and Local Government, Edukampyon Awards, and High Functional City Award for anti-drug initiatives.
b. Manila ranked 2nd Most Competitive Highly Urbanized City in the Philippines;
c. Launched CLUP 2035 and comprehensive planning documents for city zoning, investment, and development;
d. For Senior Citizens program, issuance of 43,000+ IDs, distributed 176,000 birthday cakes, and processed cash gifts to 25 centenarians and quarterly payrolls for nearly 190,000 beneficiaries.
e. The Public Employment Service Office (PESO) assisted 40,905 residents through 17 mega job fairs, 157 local recruitment events, TUPAD, SPES, GIP, livelihood programs and career guidance for over 27,000 students;
f. The Manila Sports Committee hosted more than 30 fun runs under the “Move Manila – Car-Free Sunday”
g. Kalinga sa Manila Project to six districts of Manila;
h. Distribution of monetary assistance to families affected by multiple fire incidents;
i. Distribution of Christmas food boxes to six districts of Manila;
j. Construction/ repair/ rehabilitation/ improvement/ upgrading/ installation of various structures and facilities:
• Completion of the following major infrastructure projects:
1. Construction of Pedro Gil Residences
2. Construction of San Sebastian Residences
3. Installation of Solar Studs Phase IV
4. Construction of Construction of Six (6) - Storey School Building at Emilio Jacinto Elementary School
5. Construction of Six (6) - Storey School Building at Aurora A. Quezon Elementary School
